<title>USA: Tentative agreement in Giant strike.</title>
<headline>Tentative agreement in Giant strike.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON</dateline>
<text>
<p>A tentative agreement was reached Sunday to settle the strike against Giant Food Inc., a major grocery chain in the Washington-Baltimore area, by members of the Teamsters Union, a union official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have a tentative agreement. We have a fair deal,&quot; the official told Reuters. He said a ratification vote was scheduled for Sunday afternoon and union officials were recommending approval.</p>
<p>The strike by 328 drivers and nearly 2,000 warehouse workers began Dec. 14.</p>
</text>
